#VAR(Table, TABLE)
#ADDTBL("../encoding.tbl", Table)
#ACTIVETBL(Table)
#VAR(PTR, CUSTOMPOINTER)
#CREATEPTR(PTR, "LINEAR", 0, 16)
#JMP($000026AA)

#WRITE(PTR, $00001E66)
We’d said we’d walk home together, but my base was only ten minutes from school.%NMeanwhile, Yua needed to go all the way to Shinsen Station, so%NI needed to accompany her before I could go home.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001E76)
But by force of habit, I led Yua into Shoto Park.
<LINE>
The park was something of a shortcut on my route to school, saving%Nme about a minute each way.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001EB6)
【優愛】
“So, Nishijou-kun, you eat your breakfast here in the morning,%Nright?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001EC6)
【拓巳】
“Um... Yeah...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001ED6)
How did she know that?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001EE6)
【優愛】
“Aha, I knew it! I’ve seen you eat here quite often, but I noticed%Nyou weren’t here every day.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001EF6)
【優愛】
“But it looks like I’ve finally solved that mystery!
<LINE>
It’s just because you don’t go to school every day, right?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F06)
【拓巳】
“...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F16)
【優愛】
“Oh, um, well, I’m not saying there’s anything wrong with that.%NJust that I was curious...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F26)
【拓巳】
“R-Right...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F36)
Yua suddenly stopped, turning toward the bench I always ate%Nbreakfast on.
<LINE>
Nobody was sitting there at the moment.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F76)
【優愛】
“You know, whenever I looked at you from behind while you sat here, you always looked... um... You always looked really sad...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F86)
Yua bent forward slightly, gently stroking the back of the bench.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001F96)
【優愛】
“And the more I looked at you, the more I wanted to talk to you...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001FA6)
The bench was right in front of the fence by the pond.
<LINE>
Whenever you sat on it, you could just stare out at the pond%Nwithout needing to worry about whether others might be looking at%Nyou.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001FB6)
It was right by the water mill too, making it even more%Ninconspicuous. That was another huge plus.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001FC6)
【優愛】
“Whenever I didn’t see you here,%NI got so worried that I had trouble eating...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00001FD6)
R-Really?
<LINE>
I’d never noticed her looking at me when I was here.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002016)
【優愛】
“It’s a bit silly, isn’t it?%NWorrying about someone you’ve never even spoken to...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002026)
【優愛】
“But I just couldn’t find the courage to talk to you...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002036)
So her initial stalking was an extension of that...
<LINE>
Or maybe not “stalking,” per se—maybe she’d just been looking out%Nfor me.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002076)
【優愛】
“Do you mind if we sit down here for a little?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002086)
【優愛】
“I want to see... um... the scenery you were always looking at,%NNishijou-kun...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002096)
I didn’t really have much of a reason to refuse.
<LINE>
I nodded my head, still facing out toward the lake.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000217A)
Yua placed her bag on top of the bench and quietly took a seat.
<LINE>
She then straightened her posture and gazed out at the lake.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000218A)
It was so incredibly quiet...
<LINE>
So incredibly serene...
<LINE>
And Yua was sitting right by my side.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000219A)
A gentle breeze drew ripples on the water, and it softly swayed%NYua’s hair.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000021AA)
Was this what it felt like to be a normie?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000021BA)
This situation was so ordinary, so casual... so why did I feel like I was about to cry?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000021CA)
【優愛】
“Enjoying a nice breakfast here sounds amazing...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000021DA)
I looked at the side of Yua’s face as she whispered that.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000021EA)
If life were an eroge, this is where she’d confess her love.%NThen we’d lean in, kiss, and the Good End credits would roll.%NAnd who knows, if the situation called for it, maybe we’d get%Nstraight into some *exhibitionism*... JK, fuhihi.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000021FA)
【優愛】
“Maybe I’ll give it a try sometime soon...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000220A)
Yua turned and looked up at me.
<LINE>
Unable to find the words to say, I looked down at Yua’s bag.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00002296)
Cursing my inability to maintain eye contact with a girl, I stared%Ninstead at the three Gero Froggy straps hanging from her bag.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000022A6)
【拓巳】
“...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000024AA)
Hold on...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000024BA)
Wait a minute...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000024CA)
Something about this scene... was really nagging at me...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000024DA)
And that thing was...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000024EA)
...the Gero Froggies.
<LINE>
Characters that were popular with high school girls.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000024FA)
But I’d seen those exact ones before, hadn’t I?
<LINE>
Where, though...?
<FILEEND26>
